    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0203" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24063: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tuck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-09T19:00:00-04:00">September 9,
                            1942—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>553. Your 1314, Sept. 7, 7 p.m. Report of your conversation with M. Laval as
                    given to the press here<anchor n="93" xml:id="d197-f1"/> was published in Radio
                    Bulletin no. 212 of September 8.</p>
                <p>You will make occasion to state that the American Government approves your
                    statement as the official reply to M. Laval’s protest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="93" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>For text of press release, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, September 12, 1942, p. 750.</p>
            </note>
